  "operator_reality_argument": "With real scalar spin-local potential and real ordinary-NC projectors/D in real space, complex conjugation C obeys C H_sigma(k,R,A) C^-1 = H_sigma(-k,R,-A), separately for sigma=up/down. Differentiating real ionic R gives C(dH/dR)C^-1 = dH(-k)/dR; force=-dH/dR is likewise even. Differentiating vector-potential A gives an odd physical current, including NC nonlocal terms. This is not the spin-flipping i sigma_y C operation. Spatial pullback composes these rules with S and irt. The oracle's real nonlocal finite Hamiltonian commutator current independently checks the odd sign; it is not a material-current prediction.",
  "implementation_delivery": {
    "status": "source implementation delivered; no oracle, material calculation, test, lint or build executed by worker",
